{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghZKT5cemfKe6FJS4kC3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018m4oh1KG5qJ6L4KPLKJFsB","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-011720__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","offset":99,"limit":240},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3888,"cache_read_input_tokens":22358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3888},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"b73132c8-a330-4ad2-98ae-d65a8a013755","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:17:31.282Z","request_id":"req_011CghZKSoWCRrDPEhh1iJox","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018m4oh1KG5qJ6L4KPLKJFsB":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-011720__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","offset":99,"limit":240}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018m4oh1KG5qJ6L4KPLKJFsB","type":"tool_result","content":"99\t## 2. Genre, perspective and scope\n100\t\n101\t- **Genre:** sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball), plus a light life-sim (vacation calendar, friendship, collecting),\n102\t  plus minigames (rhythm Pool Hop, casino). Matches are the heart of it, about 60% of play time.\n103\t- **Cameras:**\n104\t  - **Matches:** a custom side-on **Broadcast** view, `new E.View('court', 'Broadcast', 0, 32, 1.5, 1)`. The net runs\n105\t    into the screen at the centre, your team is on the left, and the sea is behind the court. `cam.frame` keeps the ball\n106\t    and players in shot like a TV director.\n107\t  - Alternate: **Serve Cam**, `new E.View('servecam', 'Serve Cam', ±90, 46, 1.5, 1)`, behind your team as in the\n108\t    source. Pick the yaw sign that puts your team at the bottom of the screen (check with a screenshot). V or R3 toggles\n109\t    it, and Settings has it too; the attract mode cuts between both. Tune Broadcast pitch 28–36 and scale 1.3–1.5 by\n110\t    screenshot, keeping characters at least 44 px tall at zoom 1.\n111\t  - **Resort places and the Villa:** `threequarter`. **Island map:** `iso`. **Pool Hop:** the Broadcast angle following\n112\t    the hopper.\n113\t  - **Shops, wardrobe, casino tables and album:** full-screen canvas UI over a live world view.\n114\t- **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (at least 320×240; about 427×240 on 16:9). Every HUD is anchored to\n115\t  `r.W` and `r.H`.\n116\t- **Length:** a whole vacation takes about 45–75 minutes. A Beach Match to 7 takes about 4 minutes.\n117\t- **Performance:** TASK.md makes the budget unlimited, so spend it on the look: full HD crowds, plenty of props, lights\n118\t  and particles, GPU lighting where it helps. Do no FPS or optimization work; that is out of scope.\n119\t- **Hooks for the full game:** days, slots, cast, items, locations, events, text, music and tuning are all data tables.\n120\t  Adding a day, a fighter or a shop is a data edit plus art.\n121\t\n122\t---\n123\t\n124\t## 3. Tech and architecture\n125\t\n126\t### 3.1 Stack\n127\t\n128\t- **Engine:** my-3D2dge **v0.85.2**, the handoff package at\n129\t  `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`.\n130\t  - Use the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`, which carries every module (story, songs, rhythm, arcade…).\n131\t  - Copy it to `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js` and patch it as §3.2 says.\n132\t  - Read `API.md` and `docs/ASSETS.md` whole. Grep `API-INDEX.md` and `AI_GUIDE.md` for: the sports recipe, Shell,\n133\t    Players, Audio, Testing without a browser, Recorded sessions, and \"New animation on the rigs\".\n134\t- **Kit to learn from:** `kits/sports.js` (2v2, `game.allowJoin`, the ball as a Body, `E.arc`, the crowd, radio\n135\t  commentary, the `proof()`/`bot()` pattern). Read it all. The volleyball simulation is new, but reuse its patterns.\n136\t- **Motion clips:** `src/mocap/readable.js`, `src/mocap/mocap.js`, and a small set cut with `tools/anim-set.mjs` from\n137\t  `src/mocap/sets/{quaternius,mesh2motion,cmu}.js`. Raw files are at\n138\t  `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`. The clip list is in §4.26.\n139\t- **AI Hub client:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js` (v1.4.0 when this\n140\t  was planned), pasted in **unmodified**. For tests also fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from the same\n141\t  folder. Read `lib/hub/README.md` whole.\n142\t- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;\n143\t  the handoff's `tools/check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs` and `replay.mjs`; Python 3 for the hub harness's local server.\n144\t- **Rules:** no other runtime libraries and no network at runtime. The hub client only talks to its parent frame.\n145\t- **Machine note:** `/tmp` was almost full when this was planned. If npm or Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set\n146\t  `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`.\n147\t\n148\t**Fetching the sources** (M0):\n149\t\n150\t```sh\n151\tgit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git DEV/.src/my-3d2dge\n152\tcd DEV/.src/my-3d2dge && git sparse-checkout set --no-cone /dist/handoff/ /src/mocap/mocap.js /src/mocap/readable.js \\\n153\t  /src/mocap/sets/ /src/mocap/catalogs/ /tools/anim-set.mjs /docs/MOCAP.md\n154\t# (add any file anim-set.mjs imports if it complains)\n155\tcurl -fsSL -o DEV/vendor/aihub-session.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n156\tfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL -o DEV/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n157\t```\n158\t\n159\t### 3.2 Engine patches\n160\t\n161\tAll patches go in `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js`. Mark each with `// AOA:`, list it in `DEV/ENGINE-CHANGES.md` with what\n162\tchanged and why, give it a headless test, and mention it in the About screen's Engine Feedback.\n163\t\n164\t1. **PlayStation symbols in the pixel font.** The 5×7 font table `G57` (around line 1322) lacks ✕ ○ □ △, which\n165\t   `input.label()` returns for PlayStation pads. Add them, plus ◀ ▶ for steppers.\n166\t2. **Button symbols setting.** Change the standard `glyphs` setting (around line 2999) to `{ group: 'Game', label:\n167\t   'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox',\n168\t   'Xbox A B X Y']] }`. That way it appears on the Settings screen and defaults to PlayStation, as TASK.md requires.\n169\t3. **Per-letter dialog voice.** In `Dialog`'s typing (around line 8956, `if (this.voice && …) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)`),\n170\t   when `typeof this.voice === 'function'`, call `this.voice(ch, index, pageText, this)` for **every** newly shown\n171\t   letter. Do not skip every other letter, and do not call sfx. This drives the Animalese voices (§4.24.3).\n172\t4. **Audio.**\n173\t   - (a) Add a third bus `_voxBus` under `_master`, with `audio.voiceVolume` and a standard setting `voices` (Sound\n174\t     group, slider, default .8). Add `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, which returns the GainNode, or null\n175\t     headless.\n176\t   - (b) New options for a music track:\n177\t     - `decay` (seconds): an exponential pluck envelope instead of a held note;\n178\t     - `filter: 'lowpass'` with `cutoff` (Hz);\n179\t     - `detune` (cents): a second detuned oscillator;\n180\t     - `wave`: may name an entry in `audio.instruments`, a registry of PeriodicWave partial tables `{ real: [], imag: [] }`,\n181\t       so songs can use `steel`, `marimba`, `pluck`, `bell`, `organ` and `pad` (§4.24.1).\n182\t5. **Humanoid** (the art patch, §4.25.2):\n183\t   - (a) an `athletic` entry in `BUILDS`;\n184\t   - (b) `outfit: 'swim'` with `swim: { cut, pattern, colors: { main, accent, trim }, brief }`. Also allow\n185\t     `o.pattern` on the `shirt` outfit, for Sonny's loud shirt.\n186\t   - (c) hair styles `twinbuns`, `bun`, `braid`, `bob`, `puff` and `curly`;\n187\t   - (d) hat styles `sunhat` and `visor`;\n188\t   - (e) an `extras` hook: `rig.extras = [{ at: 'head' | 'face' | 'neck' | 'hair' | 'wristL' | 'wristR', draw(g, P,\n189\t     rig, view) }]`. It is called inside `draw` with the projected anchor point and depth-sorted with the head and torso.\n190\t     Sunglasses, flowers, necklaces, masks, glasses and wristbands use it.\n191\t   - (f) bare feet: when `colors.boot === colors.skin`, draw simple feet with no boot cuff; also an optional sandal strap\n192\t     color.\n193\t   - (g) new held poses: `vready`, `bump`, `set`, `block`, `toss`, `highfive`, `clap`, `facepalm`, `peace`, `lookback`,\n194\t     `stretch`, `sit`, `sunbathe`. Build them as `cheer`, `cast` and `kneel` are built in `solvePose`: joint targets,\n195\t     arms solved with `E.ik3`, blended by `poseW`.\n196\t6. **Session combo.** Add `game.input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: while pad button 8 (Create/View) is held, button 9\n197\t   (Options/Menu) presses reach no action. This is an AI Hub rule.\n198\t7. **Touch-off mode.** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` hides touch buttons and the touch stick for good and hides the\n199\t   Touch settings group, but keeps the corner's menu button. Touch-only devices use it (§4.1.5).\n200\t8. Register the `court` and `servecam` views. Adding them to `E.VIEWS`, or making them in game code with `new E.View`,\n201\t   are both fine.\n202\t\n203\t### 3.3 Folder layout\n204\t\n205\t```\n206\t./PLAN.md                    this plan\n207\t./<GAME>.html                the deliverable (built; never edited by hand)\n208\t./exit-interview.json\n209\tDEV/\n210\t  package.json               { \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": { \"build\": \"node tools/build.mjs\", \"test\": \"node test/run.mjs\" },\n211\t                               \"devDependencies\": { \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\" } }\n212\t  README-DEV.md              how to build, run and test; conventions\n213\t  ENGINE-CHANGES.md          every engine patch: what and why\n214\t  .src/                      sparse clone of the engine repository (reference only; never bundled)\n215\t  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the patched engine\n216\t  vendor/aihub-session.js    unmodified hub client\n217\t  vendor/mocap/readable.js, mocap.js, aoa-clips.js     (the cut clip set, name AOA)\n218\t  hub/harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md      (tests only; never bundled)\n219\t  src/*.js                   game modules (§3.6), concatenated in name order\n220\t  build/game.js              generated: every src file inside one IIFE\n221\t  build/dev.html             generated: engine, vendor and build/game.js as separate <script src>, for quick looks\n222\t  tools/build.mjs            builds build/ and the deliverable\n223\t  tools/rigsheet.mjs         every fighter × suit × facing × view to test-output/rigsheet/*.png (Playwright)\n224\t  tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs, replay.mjs, asset-sheet.mjs, asset-find.mjs, asset-set.mjs   (copied from the handoff)\n225\t  test/run.mjs               THE test command (§9)\n226\t  test/lib/load.mjs, fakehub.mjs, bots.mjs, assert.mjs\n227\t  test/suites/*.test.mjs\n228\t  test-output/               screenshots, filmstrips, rig sheets (never bundled)\n229\t```\n230\t\n231\t### 3.4 Build (`node tools/build.mjs`, also `npm run build`)\n232\t\n233\t1. Concatenate `src/*.js` in lexical order into `build/game.js`, wrapped as\n234\t   `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, G = {}; window.AOA = G; /* files */ })();`. Each src file is plain code\n235\t   that adds to `G`: no import or export.\n236\t2. Write `build/dev.html`.\n237\t3. Write the deliverable html. Order matters:\n238\t   ```html\n239\t   <!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n240\t   <script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, verbatim */</script>        <!-- first script, right after meta charset (hub rule) -->\n241\t   <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"> … (the tags of §4.23)\n242\t   <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n243\t   <title>Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball</title>\n244\t   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n245\t   </head><body>\n246\t   <!-- the handoff template's #e3-boot splash div, retitled AHEAD OR ALIVE -->\n247\t   <canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n248\t   <script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n249\t   <script>/* vendor/mocap/readable.js + mocap.js + aoa-clips.js */</script>\n250\t   <script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n251\t   </body></html>\n252\t   ```\n253\t4. Escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. Add no external URL. Print the file size.\n254\t5. The build never edits the vendor client.\n255\t\n256\t### 3.5 Runtime architecture\n257\t\n258\t- **One game.**\n259\t  ```js\n260\t  G.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'court', id: 'ahead-or-alive', bg: '#0a2d3d',\n261\t    menu: hub ? false : { items, settings, quit: 'title' },\n262\t    autoPause: !hub, corner: !hub, fullscreen: hub ? false : true, touch: touchOnly ? 'never' : 'auto' })\n263\t  ```\n264\t  Here `hub = window.AIHub && AIHub.active` is known on the first line, and `items` are the pause actions of §4.2.\n265\t  Add `G.ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme })` for themed standard screens, toasts and tutorial cards. If the Shell's pause\n266\t  screen doesn't list the `menu.items`, pass them again as `screens: { pause: { actions } }`. A headless test checks the\n267\t  pause screen lists them.\n268\t- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })`): `title`, `menu`, `attract`, `charselect`, `cutscene` (runs story\n269\t  scripts), `map`, `location` (every walkable place, entered with `{ loc }`), `match`, `poolhop`, `shop`, `wardrobe`,\n270\t  `journal`, `album`, `casino` (cashier, slots, blackjack and roulette as sub-states), `dayend`, `results`, `credits`,\n271\t  `about`, `howto`, `exhibition` (setup and join), `hub` (AI Hub card and match). Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true`;\n272\t  title, menu, attract, about, credits and the hub scene are not.\n273\t- **Overlays.** `G.overlay` is a stack for the dev panel, photo mode, toasts, the touch-only notice and the attract\n274\t  watcher. Wrap every scene with `G.wrapScene(scene)`: its `update` first calls `G.overlay.update(dt)`, which returns\n275\t  true when an overlay took the input, and its `draw` ends with `G.overlay.draw(r)`.\n276\t- **State.** `G.state` is the vacation save object (§4.19), or null outside a vacation. `G.session` is the\n277\t  exhibition/hub match config. `G.unlocks` lives in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n278\t- **Tuning.** `G.T` is the live object every system reads every step. It is built from `G.TUNING` defaults (§4.22.2),\n279\t  with dev overrides from `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`.\n280\t- **Randomness.** Gameplay never calls `Math.random`; use `G.rng(stream)`:\n281\t  - `world`: schedules, moods, weather and stock (seeded per save);\n282\t  - `match`: AI rolls, net cords (seeded per match);\n283\t  - `casino`;\n284\t  - `cosmetic`: crowd, particles, voices (never affects state).\n285\t  In a hub shared world the host seeds `match` from `AIHub.rng('match')`. A test greps `src/` for `Math.random(`.\n286\t- **Event bus.** `G.bus.on/off/emit` carries `point`, `touch`, `fault`, `matchEnd`, `gift`, `affinity`, `purchase`,\n287\t  `slotEnd`, `dayEnd`, `photo` and `story`. Commentary, stats, tests and the attract director listen to it.\n288\t- **Debug handle.** `game.debug = { snapshot(), tools }` (§9.2). The dev panel's buttons call the same `tools`.\n289\t\n290\t### 3.6 Source modules (`DEV/src/`)\n291\t\n292\t| File | Holds |\n293\t| --- | --- |\n294\t| `00-core.js` | G namespace, constants, rng streams, event bus, scene wrapper, overlay stack, helpers (`G.fmtMoney` → `S$12,500`) |\n295\t| `01-tuning.js` | `G.TUNING` (every slider: default, min, max, step, group, label, unit) and difficulty presets |\n296\t| `02-data-cast.js` | fighters, hosts and staff: looks, stats, tastes, likes, voice profiles, schedules, celebration clips |\n297\t| `03-data-items.js` | swimsuits, accessories, gifts, shops and stock rotation |\n298\t| `04-data-world.js` | location maps (rows, legends, props, spots, interactables), island map, calendar, weather, events |\n299\t| `05-data-text.js` | all dialogue as `E.Story` nodes, commentary lines, UI strings, How to Play and About texts |\n300\t| `06-data-music.js` | songs (step notation), jingles, instrument tables |\n301\t| `10-input.js` | action maps per context, devices, glyph icons, prompt drawing, the touch-only gate, mouse helpers |\n302\t| `11-ui.js` | the 10-foot canvas UI kit (§4.2) |\n303\t| `12-audio.js` | SFX defines, music control and layers, ambience loops, the Animalese voice synth |\n304\t| `13-rigs.js` | the rig factory (cast + suit + accessories), extras drawers, portraits |\n305\t| `14-world-art.js` | resort `E.SHAPES` and `E.MATERIALS`, backdrops and lighting by time of day, water, effects helpers |\n306\t| `15-anim.js` | move timelines, the arm-IK overlay, celebrations and emotes, mocap glue |\n307\t| `20-ball.js` | closed-form ball flight, launches, aiming, prediction, net and ground events |\n308\t| `21-rules.js` | the referee: touches, faults, scoring, serve rotation, match end, stats |\n309\t| `22-players.js` | player entity: movement, actions, the timing judge, the human controller |\n310\t| `23-ai.js` | volleyball AI: assignment, positioning, decisions, error model, chemistry, spectacle mode |\n311\t| `24-match.js` | the Match: phases, cameras, HUD, crowd, commentary, celebrations, replay, results |\n312\t| `25-netplay.js` | AI Hub shared-world host and client sync, the card, reporting |\n313\t| `30-vacation.js` | calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, events, saves |\n314\t| `31-map.js` | the island map scene |\n315\t| `32-location.js` | the walkable location scene, NPC spots, talk menu, interactables |\n316\t| `33-shop.js` | shops, wardrobe, gift bag, journal |\n317\t| `34-story.js` | `E.Story` wiring, cutscene scripts, portraits and voices, prologue, party, endings |\n318\t| `40-poolhop.js` | Pool Hop |\n319\t| `41-casino.js` | casino floor, cashier, slots, blackjack, roulette |\n320\t| `42-photo.js` | photo mode and album |\n321\t| `50-title.js` | boot steps, title, main menu, How to Play, About & Credits |\n322\t| `51-attract.js` | the attract director |\n323\t| `52-exhibition.js` | Beach Match setup and local join |\n324\t| `53-dev.js` | the dev panel |\n325\t| `54-results.js` | match results, day end, vacation results, credits roll |\n326\t| `99-main.js` | building the game, scene registry, hub detection, boot, `game.start` |\n327\t\n328\t---\n329\t\n330\t## 4. Systems\n331\t\n332\t### 4.1 Input, devices, glyphs, prompts (`10-input.js`)\n333\t\n334\t**4.1.1 Action maps.** Each scene sets an `input` preset. Every preset includes the engine defaults for `up`, `down`,\n335\t`left` and `right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad, left stick) and for `start` and `pause`.\n336\t\n337\t| Preset | Action | Keyboard | Mouse | Pad (standard mapping) |\n338\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"e6877774-8f01-48a2-b846-90b7698d4bde","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:17:31.292Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-011720__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 2. Genre, perspective and scope\n\n- **Genre:** sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball), plus a light life-sim (vacation calendar, friendship, collecting),\n  plus minigames (rhythm Pool Hop, casino). Matches are the heart of it, about 60% of play time.\n- **Cameras:**\n  - **Matches:** a custom side-on **Broadcast** view, `new E.View('court', 'Broadcast', 0, 32, 1.5, 1)`. The net runs\n    into the screen at the centre, your team is on the left, and the sea is behind the court. `cam.frame` keeps the ball\n    and players in shot like a TV director.\n  - Alternate: **Serve Cam**, `new E.View('servecam', 'Serve Cam', ±90, 46, 1.5, 1)`, behind your team as in the\n    source. Pick the yaw sign that puts your team at the bottom of the screen (check with a screenshot). V or R3 toggles\n    it, and Settings has it too; the attract mode cuts between both. Tune Broadcast pitch 28–36 and scale 1.3–1.5 by\n    screenshot, keeping characters at least 44 px tall at zoom 1.\n  - **Resort places and the Villa:** `threequarter`. **Island map:** `iso`. **Pool Hop:** the Broadcast angle following\n    the hopper.\n  - **Shops, wardrobe, casino tables and album:** full-screen canvas UI over a live world view.\n- **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (at least 320×240; about 427×240 on 16:9). Every HUD is anchored to\n  `r.W` and `r.H`.\n- **Length:** a whole vacation takes about 45–75 minutes. A Beach Match to 7 takes about 4 minutes.\n- **Performance:** TASK.md makes the budget unlimited, so spend it on the look: full HD crowds, plenty of props, lights\n  and particles, GPU lighting where it helps. Do no FPS or optimization work; that is out of scope.\n- **Hooks for the full game:** days, slots, cast, items, locations, events, text, music and tuning are all data tables.\n  Adding a day, a fighter or a shop is a data edit plus art.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Tech and architecture\n\n### 3.1 Stack\n\n- **Engine:** my-3D2dge **v0.85.2**, the handoff package at\n  `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`.\n  - Use the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`, which carries every module (story, songs, rhythm, arcade…).\n  - Copy it to `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js` and patch it as §3.2 says.\n  - Read `API.md` and `docs/ASSETS.md` whole. Grep `API-INDEX.md` and `AI_GUIDE.md` for: the sports recipe, Shell,\n    Players, Audio, Testing without a browser, Recorded sessions, and \"New animation on the rigs\".\n- **Kit to learn from:** `kits/sports.js` (2v2, `game.allowJoin`, the ball as a Body, `E.arc`, the crowd, radio\n  commentary, the `proof()`/`bot()` pattern). Read it all. The volleyball simulation is new, but reuse its patterns.\n- **Motion clips:** `src/mocap/readable.js`, `src/mocap/mocap.js`, and a small set cut with `tools/anim-set.mjs` from\n  `src/mocap/sets/{quaternius,mesh2motion,cmu}.js`. Raw files are at\n  `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`. The clip list is in §4.26.\n- **AI Hub client:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js` (v1.4.0 when this\n  was planned), pasted in **unmodified**. For tests also fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from the same\n  folder. Read `lib/hub/README.md` whole.\n- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;\n  the handoff's `tools/check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs` and `replay.mjs`; Python 3 for the hub harness's local server.\n- **Rules:** no other runtime libraries and no network at runtime. The hub client only talks to its parent frame.\n- **Machine note:** `/tmp` was almost full when this was planned. If npm or Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set\n  `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`.\n\n**Fetching the sources** (M0):\n\n```sh\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git DEV/.src/my-3d2dge\ncd DEV/.src/my-3d2dge && git sparse-checkout set --no-cone /dist/handoff/ /src/mocap/mocap.js /src/mocap/readable.js \\\n  /src/mocap/sets/ /src/mocap/catalogs/ /tools/anim-set.mjs /docs/MOCAP.md\n# (add any file anim-set.mjs imports if it complains)\ncurl -fsSL -o DEV/vendor/aihub-session.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\nfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL -o DEV/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n```\n\n### 3.2 Engine patches\n\nAll patches go in `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js`. Mark each with `// AOA:`, list it in `DEV/ENGINE-CHANGES.md` with what\nchanged and why, give it a headless test, and mention it in the About screen's Engine Feedback.\n\n1. **PlayStation symbols in the pixel font.** The 5×7 font table `G57` (around line 1322) lacks ✕ ○ □ △, which\n   `input.label()` returns for PlayStation pads. Add them, plus ◀ ▶ for steppers.\n2. **Button symbols setting.** Change the standard `glyphs` setting (around line 2999) to `{ group: 'Game', label:\n   'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox',\n   'Xbox A B X Y']] }`. That way it appears on the Settings screen and defaults to PlayStation, as TASK.md requires.\n3. **Per-letter dialog voice.** In `Dialog`'s typing (around line 8956, `if (this.voice && …) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)`),\n   when `typeof this.voice === 'function'`, call `this.voice(ch, index, pageText, this)` for **every** newly shown\n   letter. Do not skip every other letter, and do not call sfx. This drives the Animalese voices (§4.24.3).\n4. **Audio.**\n   - (a) Add a third bus `_voxBus` under `_master`, with `audio.voiceVolume` and a standard setting `voices` (Sound\n     group, slider, default .8). Add `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, which returns the GainNode, or null\n     headless.\n   - (b) New options for a music track:\n     - `decay` (seconds): an exponential pluck envelope instead of a held note;\n     - `filter: 'lowpass'` with `cutoff` (Hz);\n     - `detune` (cents): a second detuned oscillator;\n     - `wave`: may name an entry in `audio.instruments`, a registry of PeriodicWave partial tables `{ real: [], imag: [] }`,\n       so songs can use `steel`, `marimba`, `pluck`, `bell`, `organ` and `pad` (§4.24.1).\n5. **Humanoid** (the art patch, §4.25.2):\n   - (a) an `athletic` entry in `BUILDS`;\n   - (b) `outfit: 'swim'` with `swim: { cut, pattern, colors: { main, accent, trim }, brief }`. Also allow\n     `o.pattern` on the `shirt` outfit, for Sonny's loud shirt.\n   - (c) hair styles `twinbuns`, `bun`, `braid`, `bob`, `puff` and `curly`;\n   - (d) hat styles `sunhat` and `visor`;\n   - (e) an `extras` hook: `rig.extras = [{ at: 'head' | 'face' | 'neck' | 'hair' | 'wristL' | 'wristR', draw(g, P,\n     rig, view) }]`. It is called inside `draw` with the projected anchor point and depth-sorted with the head and torso.\n     Sunglasses, flowers, necklaces, masks, glasses and wristbands use it.\n   - (f) bare feet: when `colors.boot === colors.skin`, draw simple feet with no boot cuff; also an optional sandal strap\n     color.\n   - (g) new held poses: `vready`, `bump`, `set`, `block`, `toss`, `highfive`, `clap`, `facepalm`, `peace`, `lookback`,\n     `stretch`, `sit`, `sunbathe`. Build them as `cheer`, `cast` and `kneel` are built in `solvePose`: joint targets,\n     arms solved with `E.ik3`, blended by `poseW`.\n6. **Session combo.** Add `game.input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: while pad button 8 (Create/View) is held, button 9\n   (Options/Menu) presses reach no action. This is an AI Hub rule.\n7. **Touch-off mode.** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` hides touch buttons and the touch stick for good and hides the\n   Touch settings group, but keeps the corner's menu button. Touch-only devices use it (§4.1.5).\n8. Register the `court` and `servecam` views. Adding them to `E.VIEWS`, or making them in game code with `new E.View`,\n   are both fine.\n\n### 3.3 Folder layout\n\n```\n./PLAN.md                    this plan\n./<GAME>.html                the deliverable (built; never edited by hand)\n./exit-interview.json\nDEV/\n  package.json               { \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": { \"build\": \"node tools/build.mjs\", \"test\": \"node test/run.mjs\" },\n                               \"devDependencies\": { \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\" } }\n  README-DEV.md              how to build, run and test; conventions\n  ENGINE-CHANGES.md          every engine patch: what and why\n  .src/                      sparse clone of the engine repository (reference only; never bundled)\n  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the patched engine\n  vendor/aihub-session.js    unmodified hub client\n  vendor/mocap/readable.js, mocap.js, aoa-clips.js     (the cut clip set, name AOA)\n  hub/harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md      (tests only; never bundled)\n  src/*.js                   game modules (§3.6), concatenated in name order\n  build/game.js              generated: every src file inside one IIFE\n  build/dev.html             generated: engine, vendor and build/game.js as separate <script src>, for quick looks\n  tools/build.mjs            builds build/ and the deliverable\n  tools/rigsheet.mjs         every fighter × suit × facing × view to test-output/rigsheet/*.png (Playwright)\n  tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs, replay.mjs, asset-sheet.mjs, asset-find.mjs, asset-set.mjs   (copied from the handoff)\n  test/run.mjs               THE test command (§9)\n  test/lib/load.mjs, fakehub.mjs, bots.mjs, assert.mjs\n  test/suites/*.test.mjs\n  test-output/               screenshots, filmstrips, rig sheets (never bundled)\n```\n\n### 3.4 Build (`node tools/build.mjs`, also `npm run build`)\n\n1. Concatenate `src/*.js` in lexical order into `build/game.js`, wrapped as\n   `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, G = {}; window.AOA = G; /* files */ })();`. Each src file is plain code\n   that adds to `G`: no import or export.\n2. Write `build/dev.html`.\n3. Write the deliverable html. Order matters:\n   ```html\n   <!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n   <script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, verbatim */</script>        <!-- first script, right after meta charset (hub rule) -->\n   <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"> … (the tags of §4.23)\n   <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n   <title>Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball</title>\n   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n   </head><body>\n   <!-- the handoff template's #e3-boot splash div, retitled AHEAD OR ALIVE -->\n   <canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n   <script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n   <script>/* vendor/mocap/readable.js + mocap.js + aoa-clips.js */</script>\n   <script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n   </body></html>\n   ```\n4. Escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. Add no external URL. Print the file size.\n5. The build never edits the vendor client.\n\n### 3.5 Runtime architecture\n\n- **One game.**\n  ```js\n  G.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'court', id: 'ahead-or-alive', bg: '#0a2d3d',\n    menu: hub ? false : { items, settings, quit: 'title' },\n    autoPause: !hub, corner: !hub, fullscreen: hub ? false : true, touch: touchOnly ? 'never' : 'auto' })\n  ```\n  Here `hub = window.AIHub && AIHub.active` is known on the first line, and `items` are the pause actions of §4.2.\n  Add `G.ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme })` for themed standard screens, toasts and tutorial cards. If the Shell's pause\n  screen doesn't list the `menu.items`, pass them again as `screens: { pause: { actions } }`. A headless test checks the\n  pause screen lists them.\n- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })`): `title`, `menu`, `attract`, `charselect`, `cutscene` (runs story\n  scripts), `map`, `location` (every walkable place, entered with `{ loc }`), `match`, `poolhop`, `shop`, `wardrobe`,\n  `journal`, `album`, `casino` (cashier, slots, blackjack and roulette as sub-states), `dayend`, `results`, `credits`,\n  `about`, `howto`, `exhibition` (setup and join), `hub` (AI Hub card and match). Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true`;\n  title, menu, attract, about, credits and the hub scene are not.\n- **Overlays.** `G.overlay` is a stack for the dev panel, photo mode, toasts, the touch-only notice and the attract\n  watcher. Wrap every scene with `G.wrapScene(scene)`: its `update` first calls `G.overlay.update(dt)`, which returns\n  true when an overlay took the input, and its `draw` ends with `G.overlay.draw(r)`.\n- **State.** `G.state` is the vacation save object (§4.19), or null outside a vacation. `G.session` is the\n  exhibition/hub match config. `G.unlocks` lives in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n- **Tuning.** `G.T` is the live object every system reads every step. It is built from `G.TUNING` defaults (§4.22.2),\n  with dev overrides from `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`.\n- **Randomness.** Gameplay never calls `Math.random`; use `G.rng(stream)`:\n  - `world`: schedules, moods, weather and stock (seeded per save);\n  - `match`: AI rolls, net cords (seeded per match);\n  - `casino`;\n  - `cosmetic`: crowd, particles, voices (never affects state).\n  In a hub shared world the host seeds `match` from `AIHub.rng('match')`. A test greps `src/` for `Math.random(`.\n- **Event bus.** `G.bus.on/off/emit` carries `point`, `touch`, `fault`, `matchEnd`, `gift`, `affinity`, `purchase`,\n  `slotEnd`, `dayEnd`, `photo` and `story`. Commentary, stats, tests and the attract director listen to it.\n- **Debug handle.** `game.debug = { snapshot(), tools }` (§9.2). The dev panel's buttons call the same `tools`.\n\n### 3.6 Source modules (`DEV/src/`)\n\n| File | Holds |\n| --- | --- |\n| `00-core.js` | G namespace, constants, rng streams, event bus, scene wrapper, overlay stack, helpers (`G.fmtMoney` → `S$12,500`) |\n| `01-tuning.js` | `G.TUNING` (every slider: default, min, max, step, group, label, unit) and difficulty presets |\n| `02-data-cast.js` | fighters, hosts and staff: looks, stats, tastes, likes, voice profiles, schedules, celebration clips |\n| `03-data-items.js` | swimsuits, accessories, gifts, shops and stock rotation |\n| `04-data-world.js` | location maps (rows, legends, props, spots, interactables), island map, calendar, weather, events |\n| `05-data-text.js` | all dialogue as `E.Story` nodes, commentary lines, UI strings, How to Play and About texts |\n| `06-data-music.js` | songs (step notation), jingles, instrument tables |\n| `10-input.js` | action maps per context, devices, glyph icons, prompt drawing, the touch-only gate, mouse helpers |\n| `11-ui.js` | the 10-foot canvas UI kit (§4.2) |\n| `12-audio.js` | SFX defines, music control and layers, ambience loops, the Animalese voice synth |\n| `13-rigs.js` | the rig factory (cast + suit + accessories), extras drawers, portraits |\n| `14-world-art.js` | resort `E.SHAPES` and `E.MATERIALS`, backdrops and lighting by time of day, water, effects helpers |\n| `15-anim.js` | move timelines, the arm-IK overlay, celebrations and emotes, mocap glue |\n| `20-ball.js` | closed-form ball flight, launches, aiming, prediction, net and ground events |\n| `21-rules.js` | the referee: touches, faults, scoring, serve rotation, match end, stats |\n| `22-players.js` | player entity: movement, actions, the timing judge, the human controller |\n| `23-ai.js` | volleyball AI: assignment, positioning, decisions, error model, chemistry, spectacle mode |\n| `24-match.js` | the Match: phases, cameras, HUD, crowd, commentary, celebrations, replay, results |\n| `25-netplay.js` | AI Hub shared-world host and client sync, the card, reporting |\n| `30-vacation.js` | calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, events, saves |\n| `31-map.js` | the island map scene |\n| `32-location.js` | the walkable location scene, NPC spots, talk menu, interactables |\n| `33-shop.js` | shops, wardrobe, gift bag, journal |\n| `34-story.js` | `E.Story` wiring, cutscene scripts, portraits and voices, prologue, party, endings |\n| `40-poolhop.js` | Pool Hop |\n| `41-casino.js` | casino floor, cashier, slots, blackjack, roulette |\n| `42-photo.js` | photo mode and album |\n| `50-title.js` | boot steps, title, main menu, How to Play, About & Credits |\n| `51-attract.js` | the attract director |\n| `52-exhibition.js` | Beach Match setup and local join |\n| `53-dev.js` | the dev panel |\n| `54-results.js` | match results, day end, vacation results, credits roll |\n| `99-main.js` | building the game, scene registry, hub detection, boot, `game.start` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Systems\n\n### 4.1 Input, devices, glyphs, prompts (`10-input.js`)\n\n**4.1.1 Action maps.** Each scene sets an `input` preset. Every preset includes the engine defaults for `up`, `down`,\n`left` and `right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad, left stick) and for `start` and `pause`.\n\n| Preset | Action | Keyboard | Mouse | Pad (standard mapping) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |","numLines":240,"startLine":99,"totalLines":2193}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018m4oh1KG5qJ6L4KPLKJFsB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
