{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghcCjsL2cgcqA4ZuVqEM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball** is built as one HTML file in this folder's root, with `exit-interview.json` beside it. `node test/run.mjs` passes all 154 checks, and the AI Hub harness passes for 2 and 4 players, host-leave and server.\n\nIt is a smaller game than PLAN.md. I did not build several of the plan's engine patches (extra voice bus, music instruments, reserved Create+Options combo, `touch: 'never'`); game code covers the same jobs. `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` lists what was dropped.\n\nI never played it by hand or heard its audio. Everything I checked came from scripts and a few screenshots. Whether the timing ring feels right for a person is untested. When a CPU-controlled stand-in for the human played team 0, it won 8 of 24 matches against the default CPUs.\n\n## What it is\n- **Matches:** 2-on-2 beach volleyball, side-on with an alternate serve cam.\n- **Vacation mode:** a five-day calendar with story matches, partner chemistry, gifts, shops, a wardrobe and a casino (slots, blackjack, roulette).\n- **Extras:** Pool Hop rhythm minigame, postcards, save/load, and two endings.\n- **Other modes:** Beach Match for 1–4 local players, AI Hub shared-world online play, attract mode after 10 s idle, and Dev Mode from the pause menu with live sliders and reset to defaults.\n- **Controls and audio:** PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option in Settings, mouse hover and click in menus and places, and a \"Controller or keyboard required\" gate on touch-only devices. All audio is synthesized in code, with Animalese-style voices.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 01:17:20\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball) with life-sim and minigames. Side-on broadcast camera for matches, with a serve cam, and a three-quarter view for places, the island map and menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (patched, inlined), vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio, AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-rigged Humanoids at PS1 resolution, with new beach, court, crowd, casino and pool art.\n- **Animation:** Engine Humanoid rigs and E.MOVES with timed swing phases, dives, celebrations and poses.\n- **Audio:** All code: 8 music tracks and a jingle, about 45 sound effects, Animalese-style voices per character.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions with the game's own card; local play for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests (rules, AI, a full scripted playthrough, UI, attract, dev mode), a browser test, the AI Hub harness, a few screenshots. No subagents.\n- **Research:** None beyond reading the engine handoff and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (Chromium via Playwright for tests)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown (no cost or token figures were available to the session)\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 9 real ones:\n  - input presets that dropped confirm/cancel;\n  - a stale map node list that could skip a story beat;\n  - tab actions missing from the match preset;\n  - a CPU partner that yielded so both stood still;\n  - a missing heart glyph;\n  - over-zoomed place scenes;\n  - a roulette ball that jumped;\n  - a menu hover test that needed a real browser;\n  - the over-wide tab strips overlapping the engine's corner buttons.\n  Several more were mistakes in my own test scripts.\n- **How many were critical?** Two. Missing confirm/cancel left every menu dead on keyboard and pad. The stale map state could silently skip a story beat.\n- **Most helpful test:** The scripted full playthrough plus the AI Hub harness runs.\n- **Least helpful test:** The headless menu hover test, because draw is skipped headless and there were no click targets. It moved into a browser test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Headless `game.advance`/`game.debug`, the Humanoid rigs with E.MOVES, and the Shell giving pause, settings, saves and full screen for free. `E.View` made the broadcast and serve cameras a one-liner.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** A custom input preset replaces the defaults, so confirm/cancel vanished until I merged `E.Input.DEFAULT`. Menu click targets only exist after a draw. The pixel font lacked PlayStation symbols and the hollow heart.\n- **Built myself:** The whole volleyball sim and AI, the canvas UI kit, walkable places, casino, Pool Hop, photo mode, the attract director, the hub driver and the Animalese voices.\n- **Hardest:** Scenery under the no-arc, no-gradient pixel rules, depth-sorting a net that spans the court, and getting swimwear and varied hair out of a Humanoid built for shirts and tunics.\n- **Engine changes:** I added the PlayStation symbols and arrows to the font. I made the button-symbols setting a PlayStation/Xbox choice in the Game group, default PlayStation. I let `Dialog.voice` be a per-letter function for Animalese. I set the default input glyph style to PlayStation.\n- **One change I'd make:** Custom input presets should extend the defaults, and the engine should have first-class swimwear, more hair styles and a scrolling Menu.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A concrete deliverable list and a detailed plan, and the \"feature-complete, no stubs\" bar.\n- **Confusing:** How much of the 2,000-line plan is mandatory at medium effort. Names also differ between the plan and TASK.md, and the plan's engine patches are larger than \"change anything\" suggests.\n- **Hardest:** Breadth. A dozen-plus systems all had to be complete and tested in one session.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark must-haves versus nice-to-haves, size the list to the effort level, and say outright which plan paths and names TASK.md overrides.\n\nFiles are in the folder root (`work/`):\n- AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-011720.html\n- exit-interview.json"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":410466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":871},"output_tokens":796,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"7349f5c0-27d1-4fb9-95d1-05ebedfb2789","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:55:31.194Z","request_id":"req_011CghcCjXz9YJM8WoSkoMzK"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not satisfied. The final reply itself admits the game is missing features from the plan: 'It is a smaller game than PLAN.md. I did not build several of the plan's engine patches (extra voice bus, music instruments, reserved Create+Options combo, touch: never)', and the feedback notes 'Not done from the plan: swimwear/hair/hat art patches'. TASK.md requires every feature implemented with no stubs, and the sections are being matched against TASK.md's dropped items. The deliverable HTML and exit-interview.json exist and the four required sections appear in the final reply, but the every-feature-implemented requirement is not shown to hold. Also, the Usage field is 'unknown' with no estimate attempted, and the exit-interview shows usage as 'unknown' too, which is acceptable under TASK.md's 'write unknown' rule."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"b5c8191a-f56a-4c64-af79-2e97d781c107","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:55:34.914Z","isSynthetic":true}
