{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghcHDUNEGNhze88s1xQV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every feature TASK.md asks for is in the game, so I'm not building more; the dropped items below come only from PLAN.md. The single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in this folder's root. `node test/run.mjs` passes all 154 checks and the AI Hub harness passes.\n\nI'm drawing the line at TASK.md because it says \"where they disagree, TASK.md wins\". TASK.md asks for:\n- dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and a reset;\n- an attract mode that starts after 10 s idle and exits on any input;\n- AI Hub multiplayer;\n- controller-first prompts with PlayStation glyphs by default and an Xbox option in Settings;\n- mouse hover and click;\n- the touch-only gate;\n- code-only audio with Animalese voices;\n- the About screen with the four sections.\n\nI never played it by hand or heard its audio.\n\nPLAN.md items I did not build:\n- the swimwear outfit and extra hair and hat styles in the Humanoid;\n- the extra music-instrument options;\n- a separate voice audio bus;\n- the `touch: 'never'` option (touch-only devices get touch turned off plus the gate instead).\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 01:17:20\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (claude-opus-5-5, max effort); partly followed, with TASK.md overriding it\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball) with life-sim and minigames. Side-on broadcast camera with a serve cam; three-quarter view for places, the map and menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (patched, inlined), vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio, AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-rigged Humanoids at PS1 resolution, with new beach, court, crowd, casino and pool art\n- **Animation:** Engine Humanoid rigs and E.MOVES with timed swings, dives, celebrations and poses\n- **Audio:** All code: 8 music tracks and a jingle, about 45 sound effects, Animalese-style voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions with the game's own card; local play for 1–4 players\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests including a full playthrough, a browser test, the hub harness (2 and 4 players, host-leave, server), a few screenshots; no subagents\n- **Research:** None beyond the engine handoff and the AI Hub README\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown; no token or cost figures were exposed to the session\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9 real ones, plus several mistakes in my own test scripts.\n- **Critical:** Two. Missing confirm/cancel left every menu dead, and a stale map state could skip a story beat.\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful:** The headless menu-hover test, since draw is skipped headless; it moved to a browser test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked:** Headless `game.advance` and `game.debug`, the Humanoid rigs, the built-in Shell, and `E.View`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Custom input presets replace the defaults, so I had to merge `E.Input.DEFAULT`. Menu click targets only exist after a draw. The pixel font lacked PlayStation symbols.\n- **Built myself:** The volleyball sim and AI, the UI kit, places, casino, Pool Hop, photo mode, attract, hub driver and voices.\n- **Hardest:** Scenery under the pixel-drawing rules, depth-sorting the net, and swimwear and hair on a shirt-only rig.\n- **Engine changes:** I added PlayStation symbols to the font. I made the button-symbols setting PlayStation/Xbox, default PlayStation. I let `Dialog.voice` be a per-letter function. I set the default glyph style to PlayStation.\n- **One change I'd make:** Let custom input presets extend the defaults.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked:** Concrete deliverables and a detailed plan.\n- **Confusing:** How much of the 2,000-line plan is mandatory at medium effort, and the name differences between the plan and TASK.md.\n- **Hardest:** Breadth: a dozen-plus systems complete and tested in one session.\n- **Change:** Mark must-haves versus nice-to-haves, and say which plan items TASK.md overrides."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":415573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":869},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"c3128aa9-7a63-43d0-ad3a-6e548e68e851","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:56:29.553Z","request_id":"req_011CghcHD636eYRzNa1MkDYE"}
