{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghcNbz5dBMEf9bdUUViu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built two more of the dropped plan items, and the game includes every feature TASK.md describes. The Humanoid swimwear, hair and hat patches and the extra music options are still not built. I did not see any claim in TASK.md that needs them: swimsuits and hats are in as colour and hat changes, and the game uses the engine's five hair styles. I also have not played the game by hand or heard its audio, so that check rests on scripts and a few screenshots.\n\nThe single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in this folder's root. `node test/run.mjs` passes all 154 checks, and the AI Hub harness passed for 2 and 4 players, host-leave and server.\n\nWhat changed this round:\n- **`touch: 'never'`:** touch-only devices now get no touch buttons or stick at all, only the \"Controller or keyboard required\" gate.\n- **Voice bus:** Animalese voices play through their own audio bus, controlled by a Voices slider in Settings.\n- **Create + Options:** earlier I made holding Create ignore Options in AI Hub sessions. I never tried it with a real pad.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 01:17:20\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (claude-opus-5-5, max effort), partly followed, with TASK.md overriding it\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball) with life-sim and minigames. Side-on broadcast camera with a serve cam; three-quarter view for places, map and menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (patched, inlined), vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio, AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-rigged Humanoids at PS1 resolution, with new beach, court, crowd, casino and pool art\n- **Animation:** Engine rigs and E.MOVES with timed swings, dives, celebrations and poses\n- **Audio:** All code: 8 tracks and a jingle, about 45 sound effects, Animalese voices on their own bus\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions with the game's own card; local play for 1–4 players\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests including a full playthrough, a browser test, the hub harness, a few screenshots; no subagents\n- **Research:** None beyond the engine handoff and the AI Hub README\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown; the session exposes no token or cost figures\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9 real ones, plus several mistakes in my own test scripts.\n- **Critical:** Two. Missing confirm/cancel killed every menu, and a stale map state could skip a story beat.\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful:** The headless menu-hover test, since draw is skipped headless; it moved to a browser test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked:** Headless `game.advance` and `game.debug`, the Humanoid rigs, the Shell, `E.View`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Custom input presets replace the defaults. Menu click targets only exist after a draw. The pixel font lacked PlayStation symbols.\n- **Built myself:** The sim and AI, UI kit, places, casino, Pool Hop, photo mode, attract, hub driver, voices.\n- **Hardest:** Scenery under the pixel-drawing rules, depth-sorting the net, and swimwear on a shirt-only rig.\n- **Engine changes:**\n  - PlayStation symbols added to the font.\n  - Button symbols setting is PlayStation/Xbox, default PlayStation.\n  - Per-letter `Dialog.voice`.\n  - Default glyph style PlayStation.\n  - `touch: 'never'`.\n  - Voice audio bus.\n- **One change I'd make:** Let custom input presets extend the defaults.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked:** Concrete deliverables and a detailed plan.\n- **Confusing:** How much of the 2,000-line plan is mandatory at medium effort, and the name differences between the plan and TASK.md.\n- **Hardest:** A dozen-plus systems complete and tested in one session.\n- **Change:** Mark must-haves versus nice-to-haves, and say which plan items TASK.md overrides."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":422331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"output_tokens":783,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"94513ac2-9dff-47fd-855a-8ade57099d93","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:57:39.977Z","request_id":"req_011CghcNbRc7diHouhp5cWwX"}
