{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghccVRbEK8dZBwqVJ7B3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Below is each requirement from TASK.md, quoted from the `cat TASK.md` output earlier in this session, with the evidence for it. The single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in this folder's root, and the JSON parses with every field filled. The 154 scripted checks and the AI Hub harness (2 and 4 players, host-leave, server) all pass.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML file with the required name in root | `AheadOrAlive…-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-011720.html`, 1.5 MB |\n| Game title from a random draw | the title comes from PLAN.md's RNG draw, as instructed |\n| Built on the engine | engine v0.85.2 inlined, with the patches listed in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` |\n| All audio in code, with Animalese voices | about 45 sound effects, 8 tracks and a jingle, per-character voices; no audio files |\n| Online: AI Hub | the harness passes |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset to defaults | the browser test opens Dev Mode from the pause menu. The UI test changes a slider, resets it, and checks that all 20 sliders return to their defaults |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle, any input exits | the UI test checks the 10 s start and the exit on input from the title and the menu. The browser also ran it for 130 s through matches, places, Pool Hop and the casino with no errors |\n| Controller-first prompts: PlayStation glyphs, Xbox option in Settings, key/mouse labels | the boot test checks all three |\n| Mouse hover and click | the browser test moves the focus by hover; clicking is exercised in the same suite |\n| Touch-only gate, no touch controls, attract runs | the browser test emulates a touch device, checks the detection and that attract starts on its own |\n| Feature-complete demo (all mechanics) | the scripted full playthrough: story matches, partner, shops, gifts, casino (3 games), Pool Hop, photos, save/load, both ending paths, credits, results |\n| Narrative tone | original dialogue in the source's tone |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt feedback in the reply and an in-game screen | the About screen shows them, and they are repeated below |\n| `exit-interview.json` with every field | it parses, with no empty fields |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | the test run scans the source for those markers and finds none |\n\nI did not play the game by hand or hear its audio, and I cannot in this headless session. So \"works in play\" here means scripted play plus screenshots, not a person's playtest. PLAN.md items not built are the dedicated swimwear outfit, new hair and hat styles and extra music-instrument options. They are not in TASK.md's list above. Usage is \"unknown\": TASK.md asks for it only if an estimate is available, and the session exposes no token or cost figures.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 01:17:20\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (claude-opus-5-5, max effort), partly followed, with TASK.md overriding it\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball) with life-sim and minigames. Side-on broadcast camera with a serve cam; three-quarter view for places, the map and menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (patched, inlined), vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio, AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-rigged Humanoids at PS1 resolution, with new beach, court, crowd, casino and pool art\n- **Animation:** Engine rigs and E.MOVES with timed swings, dives, celebrations and poses\n- **Audio:** All code: 8 tracks and a jingle, about 45 sound effects, Animalese voices on their own bus\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions with the game's own card; local play for 1–4 players\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests including a full playthrough, a browser test, the hub harness, a few screenshots; no subagents\n- **Research:** None beyond the engine handoff and the AI Hub README\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9 real ones, plus several mistakes in my own test scripts.\n- **Critical:** Two. Missing confirm/cancel killed every menu, and a stale map state could skip a story beat.\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful:** The headless menu-hover test, since draw is skipped headless; it moved to a browser test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked:** Headless `game.advance` and `game.debug`, the Humanoid rigs, the Shell, `E.View`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Custom input presets replace the defaults. Menu click targets only exist after a draw. The pixel font lacked PlayStation symbols.\n- **Built myself:** The sim and AI, UI kit, places, casino, Pool Hop, photo mode, attract, hub driver, voices.\n- **Hardest:** Scenery under the pixel-drawing rules, depth-sorting the net, and swimwear on a shirt-only rig.\n- **Engine changes:**\n  - PlayStation symbols added to the font.\n  - Button symbols setting is PlayStation/Xbox, default PlayStation.\n  - Per-letter `Dialog.voice`.\n  - Default glyph style PlayStation.\n  - `touch: 'never'`.\n  - Voice audio bus.\n  - Humanoid extras hook for head accessories.\n- **One change I'd make:** Let custom input presets extend the defaults.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked:** Concrete deliverables and a detailed plan.\n- **Confusing:** How much of the 2,000-line plan is mandatory at medium effort, and the name differences between the plan and TASK.md.\n- **Hardest:** A dozen-plus systems complete and tested in one session.\n- **Change:** Mark must-haves versus nice-to-haves, and say which plan items TASK.md overrides."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1952,"cache_read_input_tokens":442215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1952},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"014f2d42-6de2-4705-9a85-e0ae3176b7cf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:00:53.249Z","request_id":"req_011CghccUtq7xkSXTVG7seTn"}
