{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghcqMf8TRaxcGztmYsNF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reran the full suite this turn and all 154 checks pass. Each TASK.md requirement below maps to the suite that checks it, so the item-by-item check is now in this session.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Checked in |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML in root with the required name | build output; `ls` above |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu | `zbrowser` (a real browser opens Dev Mode from the Escape pause menu) |\n| Live sliders and reset to defaults | `ui` (a slider changes the live value, reset restores defaults, all 20 sliders reset) |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle, any input exits | `ui` (starts at 10 s, loops matches, places, Pool Hop and casino, exits on input from title and menu) |\n| AI Hub multiplayer | `tools/hubcheck.mjs` (2 players passed this session; 4 players, host-leave and server passed earlier) |\n| PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox option, key/mouse labels | `boot` |\n| Mouse hover and click | `zbrowser` (hover moves the focus) |\n| Touch-only gate, no touch controls, attract runs | `zbrowser` (emulated touch device) |\n| Feature-complete demo | `playthrough` (49 checks: story, partner, shops, gifts, casino, Pool Hop, photos, save/load, ending, credits, results) |\n| Match rules and CPU opponents | `match` |\n| Local 1–4 players | `ui` (a second player joins and a two-human match starts) |\n| Photo mode and postcards | `ui` and `playthrough` |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | the test run scans the source (no matches) |\n| `exit-interview.json` parses and is complete | parsed this session, no empty fields |\n| About screen with the four sections | built into the game's About scene (screenshot reviewed earlier) |\n\nThe single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in the root folder, not the dev subfolder.\n\nI have still not played the game by hand or heard its audio, and this headless session can't. The table is scripted evidence, not a person's playtest. PLAN.md's dedicated swimwear outfit, new hair and hat styles and extra music-instrument options are not built, and TASK.md does not list them. Usage is \"unknown\" because the session gives no token or cost figures.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 01:17:20\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (claude-opus-5-5, max effort), partly followed, with TASK.md overriding it\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball) with life-sim and minigames. Side-on broadcast camera with a serve cam; three-quarter view for places, the map and menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (patched, inlined), vanilla JavaScript, Web Audio, AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Playwright 1.63.0\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel-rigged Humanoids at PS1 resolution, with new beach, court, crowd, casino and pool art\n- **Animation:** Engine rigs and E.MOVES with timed swings, dives, celebrations and poses\n- **Audio:** All code: 8 tracks and a jingle, about 45 sound effects, Animalese voices on their own bus\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions with the game's own card; local play for 1–4 players\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests including a full playthrough, a browser test, the hub harness, a few screenshots; no subagents\n- **Research:** None beyond the engine handoff and the AI Hub README\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9 real ones, plus several mistakes in my own test scripts.\n- **Critical:** Two. Missing confirm/cancel killed every menu, and a stale map state could skip a story beat.\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful:** The headless menu-hover test, since draw is skipped headless; it moved to a browser test.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked:** Headless `game.advance` and `game.debug`, the Humanoid rigs, the Shell, `E.View`.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Custom input presets replace the defaults. Menu click targets only exist after a draw. The pixel font lacked PlayStation symbols.\n- **Built myself:** The sim and AI, UI kit, places, casino, Pool Hop, photo mode, attract, hub driver, voices.\n- **Hardest:** Scenery under the pixel-drawing rules, depth-sorting the net, and swimwear on a shirt-only rig.\n- **Engine changes:**\n  - PlayStation symbols added to the font.\n  - Button symbols setting is PlayStation/Xbox, default PlayStation.\n  - Per-letter `Dialog.voice`.\n  - Default glyph style PlayStation.\n  - `touch: 'never'`.\n  - Voice audio bus.\n  - Humanoid extras hook for head accessories.\n- **One change I'd make:** Let custom input presets extend the defaults.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked:** Concrete deliverables and a detailed plan.\n- **Confusing:** How much of the 2,000-line plan is mandatory at medium effort, and the name differences between the plan and TASK.md.\n- **Hardest:** A dozen-plus systems complete and tested in one session.\n- **Change:** Mark must-haves versus nice-to-haves, and say which plan items TASK.md overrides."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":463593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"output_tokens":759,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b145291d-9dd6-4001-ae7d-69eaa59b373e","uuid":"071b0880-4854-4b4a-b1d5-7226bc45214d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:03:45.198Z","request_id":"req_011CghcqMJ46fcDx4VW7md5r"}
